    "summary": "Blazing Eyes‑of‑the‑World jam, soaring He's Gone & tight Weather Report Suite",
    "blurb": "The September 8 1973 Nassau show delivers a blistering Eyes of the World, a soaring He's Gone and a flawless Weather Report Suite. Jerry’s articulate leads and Keith’s Hancock‑style organ solo lift the set, while Phil lays down a deep, syncopated groove.",
    "review": "On September 8, 1973 at Nassau Coliseum the Dead served up one of their most rewarding early‑’73 outings. The first set bursts open with a powerful Weather Report Suite that rolls straight into an inspired Let It Grow, and the centerpiece is undoubtedly the soaring Eyes Of The World jam where Jerry’s guitar sings and Keith’s organ takes a Hancock‑style flight. The second set keeps the momentum high with a fiery Greatest Story Ever Told, a tight China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, and a beautifully stretched He's Gone that showcases Bill’s tight groove and Phil’s deep, syncopated low‑end. Even the encore shines with a heartfelt Stella Blue leading into the raucous One More Saturday Night. Across all three available sources, the top‑grade soundboard from Wulf captures every nuance – crisp instrument separation, minimal coloration and no drop‑outs – making it the definitive listening experience for this underrated gem.",
